    "proves": "Sample cluster health 4 times over ~5 minutes to verify the cluster\ndoes not flap, lose quorum, or drop nodes during idle operation.\n\nThis is the core soak assertion: a healthy cluster must stay healthy\nwithout operator intervention. Each sample checks:\n  - cluster.health status == healthy\n  - etcd members >= 3 (quorum maintained)\n  - node count >= 5 (no nodes silently dropped)\n  - service count >= 19 (no services deregistered)\n\nFailure means the cluster is oscillating \u2014 systemd is restart-looping\na critical service, etcd is losing connectivity, or a node heartbeat\nis missing. Any instability here surfaces a real problem to investigate.",
